# Tools needed to render this project's pages for evidence (screenshots of
# rendered routes/states), beyond `bun install` / `bun run build` / `bun run
# lint` / `bun run format:check`, which a fresh worktree already covers.
#
# No `chromium-cli` binary is available in this environment. The Playwright
# Chromium browser itself is already cached at ~/.cache/ms-playwright (shared
# across worktrees, survives a fresh worktree checkout), but the `playwright`
# npm package is not a dependency of this project (it has no browser tests)
# and isn't resolvable via plain `node -e "require('playwright')"`. Installing
# it into the project's own node_modules would touch package.json/bun.lock,
# which most tasks in this repo don't own -- install it into a scratch
# directory instead (e.g. the session scratchpad) and drive the dev server
# from a small script there:
#
#   mkdir -p /tmp/pw-evidence && cd /tmp/pw-evidence && bun add playwright
#   # then a Node script: import { chromium } from "playwright"; ... page.goto /
#   # click / fill / screenshot against the `bun run dev` server.
#
# `npx playwright install chromium` is a no-op if the cache above already has
# a matching version; only run it if `chromium.launch()` fails with a missing
# executable error.
sh   mkdir -p /tmp/pw-evidence
sh   cd /tmp/pw-evidence && bun add playwright
